														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2713586">
									

<p>Looks like a word is missing in the first testing log. &quot;Reginald's second [wife] survived a mugging.&quot;</p>
<p>I don't know how I feel about &quot;created&quot; as the term for someone becoming a -B instance. &quot;Policy enacted at age XXX&quot; seems a little more in keeping with the insurance bent. Likewise &quot;incurred while holding the policy&quot; seems off compared to &quot;incurred while the policy is active&quot;. I work in insurance and it's possible that what I think of as appropriate insurance language is a little skewed by how we communicate internally; I am not suggesting that I know what the proper clinical phrase would be.</p>
<p>Overall, no vote for now. Small pieces of language that borders on non-clinical (&quot;shrieked, panicked&quot;) and the aforementioned insurance phrasing keep me from buying 100% into the writing and the idea doesn't have any super squicky implications in the log.</p>

